Datatypes:
An attribute that specifies the type of data in a column of our database-table

Most common datatypes:
Numberic : int,double,float,decimal
String   : varchar
Date     : Date
Boolean   : Boolean


Constraint:
It is a rule applied to a column
You can use multiple constraints at a time
e.g : Not null,default value,primary key,auto increment

//serial represents auto increment
create table person(id int serial primary key,name varchar(100) not null,city varchar(50) default 'lhr');



create table employees(emp_id serial primary key serial,fname varchar(100) not null,lname varchar(100) not null,email varchar(100) not null unique,dept varchar(50),salary int not null default 50000,hire_date Date not null default current_date );

